# AI Model Usage Rule

---
description: Enforces consistent AI model usage across the codebase
globs: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: true
---

## Model Selection Guidelines

### Vision and OCR Tasks
- Primary: `gpt-4o-audio-preview`
- Fallback: `gpt-4.1`

### Text Analysis and Processing
- Primary: `o4-mini` (for faster, cost-effective processing)
- Fallback: `o3` (when higher accuracy needed)

### Form Field Extraction
- Primary: `gpt-4o` 
- Fallback: `gpt-4.1`

### Text Generation and Summaries
- Primary: `o4-mini`
- Fallback: `o3`

## Current Model Usage in Codebase

### VA Form Processor
```typescript
// src/lib/va-forms/form-processor.ts
private model: string = 'gpt-4o-audio-preview'; // For OCR and vision tasks
```

### Sentiment Analysis
```typescript
// Use o4-mini for sentiment analysis
model: "o4-mini"
```

## Model Selection Criteria

1. Vision/OCR Tasks:
   - Use `gpt-4o-audio-preview` for best accuracy in form field detection
   - Fallback to `gpt-4.1` if audio preview not needed

2. Text Processing:
   - Use `o4-mini` for standard processing (faster, cost-effective)
   - Use `o3` when highest accuracy needed

3. Form Processing:
   - Use `gpt-4o` for general form understanding
   - Use `gpt-4.1` for complex form logic

4. Real-time Features:
   - Use `gpt-4o-realtime-preview` for streaming responses
   - Use `gpt-4o-mini-realtime-preview` for cost-effective streaming

## Implementation Notes

1. Always specify model versions explicitly
2. Use constants for model names to ensure consistency
3. Document any model changes in commit messages
4. Test performance impact when changing models

